			<div class="content" id="post-content-4509143">
									

<p>I think the larger point being made here is that this concept could sit comfortably in the confluence of &quot;escalating containment logs&quot; and &quot;simple concept taken to a logical extreme&quot;, <a href="/things-what-do-a-thing-an-essay-on-things">as described in this essay</a>.</p>
<p>That said, you don't really need to focus on testing every possibility if the point of the article is the final twist at the end. An audience is less interested in an anomaly and more in the story it tells, which may be one and the same.</p>

